# Review: CodePlugin

129 items: 24 done, 67 untested, 11 partial, 10 diverged, 17 missing. The review read the working tree on top of
the commit above, including the uncommitted move of spec sync onto plugin-file-system's `FileSystem`. Most items
are untested, not broken. The code matches the spec, but no test runs it: no test invokes an operation handler,
mounts CodeArticle, CodeSettings or SpecArticle, or loads the Coder skill. The tests that exist cover the compiler
(`compileEntry`, `bundleEntry` and `executeScript`), the sync helpers (source keys, `reconcile`, repo roots), the
review model, and three stories with play functions (ReviewPanel, SpecChangelog, DefinitionGraph). Most compiler
tests are tagged `manual`, so default CI skips them.

Of the 19 acceptance scenarios and QA tests, none is exercised end to end. Three are partly exercised: T-15, T-16
and T-18 have their build and run steps covered by compiler tests that bypass the operations. T-4 is diverged,
because its only test drives a different view switcher. The other 15, including QA-1, are not exercised.

The spec-sync move holds up. `importSpec`, `listLocalSpecs`, the `SpecSync` capability and the review reader all
go through `FileSystem.get()`. The dev route is now `/__dx/fs`, with `DX_FS_ROOTS`, and it refuses writes that are
not `.mdl`. The editor review chips (F-16.5, F-16.6) are now installed in SpecArticle and SpecChangelog: one row per
item, and scenario lines carry test chips. The biggest divergence is still in the oldest features. F-1.4 and F-3
describe a CodeArticle that edits the Spec behind a Spec | Code toggle. In the code, SpecArticle is the Spec IDE and
CodeArticle is the file browser. The credentials story (F-4, `CodeSettings`, `Credentials`) also diverged.

Gaps that matter:

- No operation has a handler test, so every Coder tool and both sync operations are untested. T-7 to T-14 and T-17
  describe exactly these tests.
- `bundleEntry` calls `esbuild.initialize({})` with no `wasmURL`. Multi-file builds probably fail in the browser.
  They pass only in the manual Node tests.
- In `plugin CodePlugin`, NavigationTargetResolver is described as resolving github: keys. It maps CodeProject
  objects to graph paths.
- `readFile` fails with `CodeOperationError`, not `FileNotFound`. The SpecArticle editor has no `mdlLint` or
  `mdlComplete`. A new CodeProject's Spec is not empty.

